<title>GERMANY: VW sees no long-term impact from stoppage.</title>
<headline>VW sees no long-term impact from stoppage.</headline>
<dateline>WOLFSBURG, Germany 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Volkswagen AG said on Tuesday that it expected virtually no long-term sales losses from a suspension in production of some models due to the ongoing Spanish trucker strike.</p>
<p>A VW spokesman said the loss in production would later be made up through additional shifts.</p>
<p>VW has been forced to stop production of its Polo model in Germany since parts cannot be delivered from Spanish suppliers, affecting about 3,500 workers.</p>
<p>The carmaker builds about 1,000 of the subcompact Polos each day.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
